From 759e9c39e3f4851f4205fdb37e8b871ef66203e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basin Battle <basin@battle>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:34:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Weapons that glow red for a blow no guard stops; the hero's
 weapon back in hand after a spell; a gentler coil

SetUnitWeaponGlow(unit, "RRGGBB", seconds) tints the unit's hand models that colour, pulsing,
for that long (a unit holding none: its whole body), over any aura's tint; nil ends it.
HasActionCombat() is 6.

While an add-on drives the action layer our own body takes the server's sheath byte, as a
remote one does: a spell clip's stow or a throw's ranged draw used to leave the melee weapon
put away for good, since no auto-attack draws it here.

A creature's coiled wind-up spreads its extra time between the way into the coil (40%) and the
creep through it, so the held pose never looks like time stopped.
